  "body": "## Summary\n\nCut release fails when its integration command runs without the required Firebase Auth emulator. Current master includes the merged prompt-resource extraction but retains that direct call. Reuse the maintained demo-emulator wrapper while keeping every PostgreSQL and authentication test mandatory.\n\nA manual **validation_only** option runs the same source-validation boundary on a selected branch with disposable PostgreSQL. It uses read-only checkout permissions without persisted credentials; every candidate, registry and provider/release job is excluded. Normal releases remain restricted to master. Existing PR CI is unchanged.\n\nCloses #45.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- **Current base to proposed source:** after integrating master `7688118`, the [exact-head validation-only run](https://github.com/MChartier/little-say/actions/runs/37872957939/job/113634941431) passed **325 unit tests, all 25 PostgreSQL/Auth integration tests, types and builds**, including source-free prompt-bundle coverage. Emulator/database cleanup completed; all six release jobs were skipped.\n- **Affected runtime and failure boundaries:** 11 targeted local tests passed for prompt payloads, resources, source-free ESM execution and validation guards. The original six missing-emulator failures, regression rejection of the old command, and real local failure/cleanup evidence remain applicable to unchanged validation code. [Actual-base impact analysis, raw results and preserved original body](https://github.com/MChartier/little-say/blob/67ca22a9dbb9b7f31bd73e5145b394529455c8cf/impact-master7688118/README.md).\n\n[Current PR CI passed](https://github.com/MChartier/little-say/actions/runs/37872940191), including five account-browser scenarios. The prior review-bot [quota refusal](https://github.com/MChartier/little-say/pull/46#issuecomment-6072598630) is retained; it is not a completed review of this head. Independent review/QA remains required.\n\nThis non-UI change validates the real source-check boundary, **not a complete release**: candidate creation/retirement, signing, providers, publishing and deployment were not exercised. PR42's retained evidence covered normal CI and release safeguards but missed this separate command path. Earlier run37871534382 remains evidence for its original source, not the new combined build.\r\n",
